       "text": "Here is a precise breakdown of the bug, where it lived, and how it was fixed.\n\n---\n\n## The V38 `fieldConfig.defaults.custom` Drop Bug\n\n### Where the bug
     was\n\n[`apps/dashboard/pkg/migration/schemaversion/v38.go`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/grafana/grafana/-/blob/apps/dashboard/pkg/migration/schemaversion/v38.go) — the `processPanelsV38`
     function.\n\n### The buggy logic (before commit `26d36ec`)\n\nThe original code used a chain of early-exit type assertions before calling `migrateOverrides`:\n\n```go\n// BUGGY original code\ndefaults, ok
     := fieldConfig[\"defaults\"].(map[string]interface{})\nif !ok {\n    continue  // skip entire panel if defaults missing\n}\n\ncustom, ok := defaults[\"custom\"].(map[string]interface{})\nif !ok {\n
     continue  // skip entire panel if defaults.custom missing ← BUG\n}\n\n// Migrate displayMode to cellOptions\nif displayMode, exists := custom[\"displayMode\"]; exists {\n    ...\n}\n\n// This line was
     ONLY reached if defaults.custom existed\nmigrateOverrides(fieldConfig)\n```\n\nThe `continue` on the `defaults[\"custom\"]` assertion caused `migrateOverrides` to **never be called** for panels where
     `fieldConfig.defaults.custom` was absent or empty — even if those panels had overrides containing `custom.displayMode` properties that needed migration. Those override `displayMode` values were silently
     left in the old format.\n\n### The fix (commit [`26d36ec`](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/github.com/grafana/grafana/-/commit/26d36ec7ffbc16df82cab8098a6e8ce5de7fe4f7))\n\nThe fix restructures the two
     concerns — defaults migration and overrides migration — so that `migrateOverrides` is **always called unconditionally**, while defaults migration is gated only when the relevant fields exist:\n\n```go\n//
     FIXED code — current state in v38.go lines 115–131\n\n// Process defaults.custom if it exists\nif defaults, ok := fieldConfig[\"defaults\"].(map[string]interface{}); ok {\n    if custom, ok :=
     defaults[\"custom\"].(map[string]interface{}); ok {\n        // Migrate displayMode to cellOptions in defaults\n        if displayMode, exists := custom[\"displayMode\"]; exists {\n            if
     displayModeStr, ok := displayMode.(string); ok {\n                custom[\"cellOptions\"] = migrateTableDisplayModeToCellOptions(displayModeStr)\n            }\n            delete(custom,
     \"displayMode\")\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Update any overrides referencing the cell display mode\n// This must be called regardless of whether defaults.custom
     exists\nmigrateOverrides(fieldConfig)\n```\n\n### The `migrateOverrides` function\n\n[Lines
     135–176](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/grafana/grafana/-/blob/apps/dashboard/pkg/migration/schemaversion/v38.go?L135-L176) walk `fieldConfig.overrides[]`, find any property with `id ==
     \"custom.displayMode\"`, rename it to `\"custom.cellOptions\"`, and convert its string value using `migrateTableDisplayModeToCellOptions`.\n\n### The `migrateTableDisplayModeToCellOptions`
     converter\n\n[Lines 178–209](https://demo.sourcegraph.com/r/github.com/grafana/grafana/-/blob/apps/dashboard/pkg/migration/schemaversion/v38.go?L178-L209) maps the legacy flat string to a structured
     object:\n\n| Legacy `displayMode` | New `cellOptions` |\n|---|---|\n| `\"basic\"` | `{ type: \"gauge\", mode: \"basic\" }` |\n| `\"gradient-gauge\"` | `{ type: \"gauge\", mode: \"gradient\" }` |\n|
     `\"lcd-gauge\"` | `{ type: \"gauge\", mode: \"lcd\" }` |\n| `\"color-background\"` | `{ type: \"color-background\", mode: \"gradient\" }` |\n| `\"color-background-solid\"` | `{ type: \"color-background\",
     mode: \"basic\" }` |\n| anything else | `{ type: <original string> }` |\n\n### Summary\n\nThe root cause was that the two migration concerns — (1) migrating `defaults.custom.displayMode` and (2)
     migrating overrides — were coupled inside a single linear chain of assertions. If a panel had no `defaults.custom` (entirely valid), the `continue` short-circuited the entire panel loop iteration,
     silently skipping override migration. The fix decouples them into independent conditional blocks and moves `migrateOverrides` outside any guard condition.\nLink:
     https://demo.sourcegraph.com/deepsearch/e51de931-71cb-41b3-ac98-410ce83d1af2\nDeep search complete — results returned."
