  The Bug Details

  Location: apps/dashboard/pkg/migration/schemaversion/v38.go:90-132 in processPanelsV38()

  Root Cause: The function had a logic error where it would skip migrateOverrides() calls for panels lacking fieldConfig.defaults.custom. When a panel had overrides containing custom.displayMode properties but
  no defaults.custom, those overrides were silently left unmigrated.

  Key Functions:

  1. V38() (line 75) — Entry point, sets schemaVersion and calls processPanelsV38()
  2. processPanelsV38() (line 90) — The buggy function that processes panels recursively. The fix moved migrateOverrides(fieldConfig) outside the conditional guards so it's always called (line 131)
  3. migrateOverrides() (line 136-176) — Migrates override properties from old custom.displayMode format to new custom.cellOptions format
  4. migrateTableDisplayModeToCellOptions() (line 179-209) — Converts legacy displayMode strings to structured cellOptions objects:
    - "gradient-gauge" → { type: "gauge", mode: "gradient" }
    - "color-background" → { type: "color-background", mode: "gradient" }
    - etc.

  The fix ensures migrateOverrides() is called unconditionally for all table panels, regardless of whether defaults.custom exists.

